# Iridium NEXT satellite (ELiTeBus-1000 bus), modelled from published
# dimensions rather than traced from any CAD data.  This file is the bus with the propulsion module and the cross link boxes;
# iridium-bus.obj, iridium-panels.obj and iridium-antenna.obj together are
# the satellite, sharing one coordinate frame, so the demo stands all three
# with the same transform.
#
#   bus                half hexagonal prism, 3.1 x 1.5 x 1.5 m
#   solar wings        two panels a side, 9.4 m tip to tip
#   main antenna       1.4 x 1.4 m L-band array, on the face to Earth
#
# Sources: eoportal.org Iridium NEXT spacecraft table (3.1 x 2.4 x 1.5 m
# stowed, 9.4 m deployed span, 860 kg), Iridium Communications investor
# materials (four solar panels, 9.4 m span), FCC IBFS SAT-MOD-2013-1227
# orbital debris plan (two solar array panels on two-axis drives).
#
# Coordinates are bpp scene units, not metres: 1 unit = 637.1 km, so the
# 9.4 m wingspan comes out at 0.376 units against the Earth's radius of
# 10 units -- the model is drawn about 25,000 times life size, because a
# real satellite would be a few tens of micrometres wide on this stage.
# (metres x 0.04 = units)
#
# Axes: +x along track (direction of travel), +y across track, +z up;
# the main mission antenna faces -z, which the demo points at the Earth's
# centre.  Faces are triangles; each corner carries its face's own normal,
# so the shading stays flat, and its own texture coordinate: each face
# spans 0..1 of the texture once (planar projection), so the demo's
# textures tile per face.
